  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 1947, something is said to have crashed near Roswell, New Mexico, and people have argued ever since about what it was. An online commentator who goes by UAPGerb, speaking on Jesse Michels's podcast, points to a man named Philip J. Corso, who he says claimed the crash happened because clashing radio signals confused the craft's navigation. If true, it would mean ordinary human radio could bring down a craft that was not ours."
